    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Frédéric Chopin (1810–1849) composed almost exclusively for piano — nocturnes, mazurkas, polonaises, études, ballades, and preludes that redefine touch and colour."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "technique",
      "title": "Technique",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Singing right-hand lines over harmonic left-hand patterns. Revolutionary pedalling. Études address specific technical problems while remaining concert pieces."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rubato",
      "title": "Rubato",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Flexible timing within steady pulse — melody breathes while harmonic framework holds. Parallels oral-tradition phrasing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "national-dances",
      "title": "National dances",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Mazurkas and polonaises embed Polish triple-meter dances in concert music — model for folk-in-classical fusion."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
